-- title:
--   Original BV random stopped-prefix physical Taylor error has vanishing mean on every finite horizon
-- statement:
--   On authentic original BV Levy X and admissible dividend D, every finite horizon T admits the original random stopped-prefix physical C1 Taylor error L1 positive convergence certificate. True jump-removed Y increments, sample-dependent grid endpoints ≤T, right-limit reserve, local compact-subcap C1 band, and a.e. shrinking increment condition are retained. The original all-clock |drift|T+|T drift-X(T)| envelope replaces the earlier unit-horizon L1 restriction. The unique ruin/contact cell remains a separate obligation.

